        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Many years ago, the great critic and journalist H. L. Mencken wrote this warning to anyone who would dare write a book on style:",
            "block_bbox": [
                91,
                623,
                783,
                673
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 4,
            "global_block_id": 4,
            "global_group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    91.0,
                    623.0
                ],
                [
                    783.0,
                    623.0
                ],
                [
                    783.0,
                    673.0
                ],
                [
                    91.0,
                    673.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "With precious few exceptions, all the books on style in English are by writers quite unable to write. The subject, indeed, seems to exercise a special and dreadful fascination over school ma’ams, bucolic college professors, and other such pseudoliterates. … Their central aim, of course, is to reduce the whole thing to a series of simple rules—the overmastering passion of their melancholy order, at all times and everywhere.",
            "block_bbox": [
                125,
                687,
                755,
                835
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 5,
            "global_block_id": 5,
            "global_group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
