            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Mencken was right: no one learns to write well by rule, especially those who cannot see or feel or think. But many people do see clearly, feel deeply, and think carefully but still cannot write sentences that make their thoughts, feelings, and visions clear to others. And the more clearly we write, the more clearly we see and feel and think. Rules help no one do that, but some principles can.",
            "block_bbox": [
                90,
